{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said: these fifteen songs correspond to fifteen ascents. He also said it is possible that it concerns melodies in a high voice. I have already mentioned at the beginning of the book what appears to be a piyyut, and this song would be sung to the pleasantness of the ascents. The name of the poet is not mentioned. Perhaps by the holy spirit it was spoken concerning the people of our exile, who are in distress and do not know what to do, only to call upon the honored HaShem."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 120, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:05.561413459Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}